LeetCode  – Search Insert Position

Approach: Binary Search

Problem:
Find the index of the target in a sorted array. If the target is not present, return the index where it should be inserted.

code --
class Solution {
    public int searchInsert(int[] nums, int target) {

        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        while (left <= right) {

            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                return mid;
            }
            else if (nums[mid] < target) {
                left = mid + 1;
            }
            else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return left;
    }
}

Approach

1. Initialize "left = 0".
2. Initialize "right = nums.length - 1".
3. Calculate the middle index.
4. If the middle element equals the target, return its index.
5. If the middle element is smaller, search the right half.
6. If the middle element is greater, search the left half.
7. When the loop ends, return "left".

Complexity

- Time Complexity: O(log n)
- Space Complexity: O(1)

Key Learning
Binary Search reduces the search area by half in every iteration.
